config ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE
    bool "Expose Zephyr settings via ZMK Studio RPC"
    depends on ZMK_STUDIO
    depends on SETTINGS
    # nanopb is normally pulled in by ZMK_STUDIO, but select it explicitly so the
    # shared proto/dispatch builds regardless of how it is reached.
    select NANOPB
    help
      Enables the setting_expose custom Studio RPC subsystem, which allows
      a connected ZMK Studio web UI to list, read, write, and delete Zephyr
      settings stored on the device.

      The subsystem requires the ZMK Studio unlock command (SECURED security
      level) to prevent unauthorized access to device settings.

if ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE

config ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE_UNIT_TEST
    bool "Run setting_expose RPC unit tests at boot (for testing only)"
    depends on LOG
    help
      When enabled, a SYS_INIT function exercises the setting_expose RPC
      handler at boot and logs PASS/FAIL results for each test case.
      This option is intended for automated testing only.

endif

#
# Split support. This is deliberately NOT nested under ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE: the
# split *peripheral* image has no ZMK_STUDIO (so ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE is off
# there) yet must still build the shared dispatch + relay to answer the
# central's relayed requests. Enable this on BOTH halves.
#
config ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE_SPLIT
    bool "Relay setting_expose requests to the split peripheral half/halves"
    depends on ZMK_SPLIT
    depends on SETTINGS
    default y
    select ZMK_SPLIT_RELAY_EVENT
    # The peripheral answers relayed requests with the shared nanopb dispatch
    # but has no ZMK_STUDIO to pull nanopb in, so select it.
    select NANOPB
    help
      On a split keyboard, let the ZMK Studio web UI address the peripheral
      half/halves via the Request `target` field: the central relays the
      request over the ZMK split event-relay, each peripheral runs it against
      its OWN settings store, and the reply is delivered back to the client as
      an RPC notification. A `target = all` delete/clear_all deletes the
      peripherals first and the central last (after every peripheral replies or
      a timeout elapses), then notifies completion.

      Both halves must be built with this option. The central additionally
      needs ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE (the Studio RPC handler); the peripheral only
      needs this option to answer relayed requests. Set to n to keep the module
      central-only and avoid the extra relay characteristic and RAM.

if ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE_SPLIT

config ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE_RELAY_STACK_SIZE
    int "Stack size (bytes) for the setting_expose relay work queue"
    default 4096
    help
      The relay work queue decodes/encodes protobuf and -- on the central --
      raises Studio RPC notifications, which synchronously build large
      notification + response structs and run a double pb_encode. Doing that on
      the shared system work queue (which the split relay receive path already
      runs on) overflows its stack, so the relay hands the heavy work to its own
      thread. Sized like the Studio RPC thread. Raise it if you see a stack
      overflow in the "se_relay" thread.

config ZMK_SETTING_EXPOSE_DELETE_ALL_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "Timeout (ms) waiting for peripheral replies before deleting the central"
    default 3000
    help
      For a `target = all` delete/clear_all the central deletes its own store
      only after every peripheral has replied. ZMK exposes no reliable count of
      *connected* peripherals, so this timeout bounds the wait: once it elapses
      the central deletes its store and emits the completion notification even
      if a peripheral (e.g. a disconnected half) never replied.

# A single relayed reply carries an encoded Response up to SE_RELAY_REPLY_DATA_MAX
# bytes (one Read / one-entry List page with a 256-byte value). Raise the
# reassembled relay payload ceiling to fit it; the relay transport chunks it
# across the split link automatically. If this default does not take effect for
# your build, set CONFIG_ZMK_SPLIT_RELAY_EVENT_DATA_LEN=512 explicitly --
# include/zmk/setting_expose/relay.h BUILD_ASSERTs it.
config ZMK_SPLIT_RELAY_EVENT_DATA_LEN
    default 512

endif
